# TURN relay for netplay.
#
# Without this, two players can only connect when at least one of them is on a
# network that lets an inbound packet through. On a LAN that always works. Across
# the internet it is a coin flip, and on mobile networks (carrier-grade NAT) it
# essentially never works — ICE fails with "add a TURN server" and the game
# cannot connect.
#
# Copy to .env (which is gitignored) and fill in. Vite inlines these AT BUILD
# TIME, so you must rebuild after changing them.
#
# A TURN credential shipped to a browser is readable by anyone who opens
# devtools. That is inherent to a static site — there is nowhere to hide it. Use
# a credential dedicated to this game, rate-limited, and rotate it if abused.
# Do NOT reuse a credential that guards anything else.

VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:turn.example.net:3478?transport=udp,turn:turn.example.net:3478?transport=tcp,turns:turn.example.net:5349
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=mountainfighters
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=change-me
